The W01 spec and its four companion files are written, and the quality checklist passes. No code was modified and nothing was committed. There was no `.specify/extensions.yml`, so no hooks ran. I also repointed `.specify/feature.json` at `specs/web/W01-auth-account`; it had been pointing at S55.

- **Directory**: `specs/web/W01-auth-account/`
- **Spec**: `spec.md`: 67 acceptance scenarios (AS-01 to AS-67) in 11 stories, 60+ functional requirements, and the Cross-capability contracts section. Every `W01` row of the pattern map (P0504, P0512, P0903) maps to requirements and scenarios.
- **Test plan**: `test-plan.md` has 67 rows, one per scenario, and names the test file for each.
- **Questions**: `questions.md` has 17 `[BREAKING]`, 13 `[CONTRACT]` and 17 `[LOCAL]` lines.
- **Gaps**: `gaps.md` lists the current code's problems with file and line references, the missing backend endpoints, and the test-tooling gaps.
- **Checklist**: `checklists/requirements.md` passes 16 of 16 items, with two notes. The spec names TanStack Query, `lib/api` and the cookie and header names because your brief and constitution VI require them. The requirements are written for the implementation agent, not for non-technical readers. The checks found no `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION]` markers, and every scenario has a test-plan row.

Decisions to review first:

- **Missing S48 endpoints**: Once no token lives in browser JavaScript, browser calls to cart, checkout, sessions and MFA need the BFF to attach the token server-side. S48 doesn't specify that forwarding today (contract C-FWD). The role-change refresh also needs `POST /api/bff/session/refresh` (C-REFRESH).
- **Google sign-in**: S02's callback sets its own cookies, so a Google user would be signed in at the API but signed out in the UI. I specified the Google UI but gated it behind `AUTH_OIDC_ENABLED` until S48 and S02 unify the session (C-OIDC).
- **No auto sign-in after register**: S01 returns the same 202 for new and existing addresses, and an automatic sign-in would reveal which addresses exist. This differs from S01's assumption that the web client logs in automatically, so it is a `[CONTRACT]` question.
- **Reset link token in the URL fragment**: The link becomes `/reset-password#token=…` instead of `?token=…`, which contradicts S28's catalogue.
- **Other findings**:
  - Log in and Sign up are unreachable on mobile today.
  - Forgot-password swallows every error and always claims "sent".
  - The MFA challenge travels in the URL.
  - `packages/contracts` has no source yet.

Questions for you:

- Is it acceptable that W01 makes the BFF forwarding (C-FWD) a hard dependency? Without it, removing the in-memory token breaks every authenticated browser call.
